{"kind":"report","text":"Approved exact head 8880a2b51eaa25aef0849e7d1bbafbd2be130cb9, resting on all 21 artifacts with docs/protocol.md 36822123 first. This resolves review 09c01bf9 and completes the required contract amendment for Lane C.\n\nArchitecture: approved. Contract owns PathOwners, ReplayContext and its parts, CheckCarryFacts, aggregate limits/accounting and ProfileStamp; policy uses those types without local shadows. R-POL-12 pins and retains immutable activated documents. R-EVAL-9 defines sequential calls with one meter per act and independent concurrent acts. The documented contract gaps are resolved or explicitly kept open.\n\nThe reservation boundary is now concrete: admission evaluates stage land; preparation evaluates the prospective stage reservation input before ready; only a passing preparation returns RetainedLandInput. Reservation rebuilds current state with that same stage and compares canonical bytes synchronously. Its no-await transaction neither evaluates policy nor hashes through WebCrypto. The bare input guard remains separate from complete replay context and its digest, so starting budget differences do not create false state mismatches.\n\nSecurity: approved for this amendment. A reservation-only blocking rule cannot be bypassed by substituting the admission stage. Current authority, evidence, policy, generation, lease and main checks remain mandatory at reservation. The repaired safe ownership and historical evidence boundaries are preserved. Retained bytes are room-internal, associated with the passing preparation and trusted storage; a caller must not supply or replace them.\n\nSimplification: approved. One prospective reservation input and one synchronous canonical comparison remove competing interpretations. Type comments, protocol rules, the section 23 acceptance case and README agree. The runtime adds a small reusable guard rather than a new policy evaluation inside the transaction.\n\nValidation: strict workspace typecheck passed. All 157 candidate tests passed on Node and all 157 on workerd, including the prior replay/ownership/authority cases and the three new reservation cases. Two additional checker-only tests passed on both hosts: mutation during await cannot change retained canonical bytes/digest, full reservation result replays, and different starting budget contexts retain the same bare guard while object key order is canonicalized. Those tests exist only in /tmp/artroom-checker-contract-amend-v2.\n\nRoom and landing implementations still need to implement and test this contract; approval here is not a claim that those runtimes exist. Open points 30–32 remain explicit. Full functional scope remains the target; schedule estimates do not constrain it.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:3682212347d2587fe5b8e0014b84580cf7e34d00","binding":"assigned","head":"8880a2b51eaa25aef0849e7d1bbafbd2be130cb9","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:ebde38abc2b2f1f9cb373ca2c43cae374c5a9fb3\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:28f1d95a74157ef3a6d31f7212140123f9e4a236\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:ebde38abc2b2f1f9cb373ca2c43cae374c5a9fb3","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}